read + findings), but\n23\t**every Anchor Gandalf run is honestly stamped `degraded: true` (\"model-narrated; not seam-validated\")**\n24\tand the tab/CLI surface that stamp prominently â€” never dressed up as full-rigor. Full Node-seam integration\n25\tis **Grasscatched to v2** (it would mean re-hosting the skill's runtime â€” beyond \"integration glue\").\n26\tAnchor does NOT re-ground or second-guess Gandalf's verdict (that would reimplement the skill); it presents\n27\tit AS Gandalf's advisory read with the honesty stamps shown.\n28\t\n29\t## Locked decisions (do not relitigate without flagging)\n30\t1. **Engine = invoke the existing Gandalf skill by EMBEDDING ITS PROTOCOL in the prompt** (resolves\n31\t   BLOCKER B: `/gandalf` is NOT auto-discoverable â€” not in `~/.claude/skills`, no SKILL.md frontmatter).\n32\t   `gandalf.py` reads `SKILL.md` from a configurable skill dir (`ANCHOR_GANDALF_SKILL_DIR`, default\n33\t   `C:\\Dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\gandalf`) and builds a prompt = the skill protocol + \"analyze the project\n34\t   at `<folder>` and emit ONLY the committed schema JSON as your final message.\" Invoked through\n35\t   `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD` (prod â†’ `claude -p`; tests â†’ `tests/stub_gandalf.py` emitting one compact schema\n36\t   JSON in a `result` envelope). This is \"using the existing skill\" (its protocol/reasoning), not\n37\t   reimplementing it, and is self-contained (no external-repo install, no symlink, fully stub-testable).\n38\t2. **Analysis input = point Gandalf at the project FOLDER** (John). The run is launched with\n39\t   `cwd = <folder>` AND `--add-dir <folder>` so Gandalf can READ the project (resolves MAJOR S1-5: the\n40\t   default argv grants only `--add-dir <output_dir>`), under a **Gandalf-specific injectable timeout**\n41\t   (`ANCHOR_GANDALF_TIMEOUT`, default e.g. 600s â€” NOT summarizer's 60s) â€” an honest degraded run on timeout,\n42\t   never a hang.\n43\t3. **Output = a full run â†’ artifacts at the PROJECT ROOT (resolves BLOCKER A)**, under\n44\t   `<folder>/gandalf/run-<ts>/`: `report.md` (full rendered schema), `exec-summary.md` (verdict + top\n45\t   findings-by-severity + top elevations) â€” **served by the existing `/artifact` route** (project-root rel\n46\t   paths, NEVER under `.anchor`, which `/artifact` hard-rejects) â€” plus `advisor-output.json` (the raw\n47\t   schema, audit truth). The internal **index** lives at `.anchor/projects/<id>/gandalf/index.json` (read\n48\t   directly by the GET endpoint, never served via `/artifact`). `gandalf/` is added to the project\n49\t   `.gitignore` (best-effort) so regenerable analysis doesn't clutter git status. The **one-line verdict**\n50\t   is the cleaned top-level `verdict` field (`summarizer.short_summary_text`, conservative cap + ellipsis),\n51\t   stored IN `index.json` (no separate `verdict.txt`). Honesty stamps (`cross_model:false`, `degraded:true`)\n52\t   are stored on the index entry and surfaced as chips.\n53\t4. **Cadence = first scan + manual.** First-ever run scheduled via a NEW `_trigger_gandalf(...)` that\n54\t   **mirrors `anchor_gui._trigger_project_summary` exactly** (resolves MAJOR S1-4): checks the module flag\n55\t   `_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY_ENABLED` (off in tests), snapshots the runner env (`ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD` + `STUB_*`/\n56\t   `FAKE_*`) and forwards it to `job_runner.launch(env=...)`, runs in a daemon thread, never blocks render.\n57\t   Hooked into the register/open/rescan block (~`anchor_gui.py:933`). First-run-ONLY via\n58\t   `run_gandalf_if_absent` guarded by a **per-project in-process lock** (`{pid: threading.Lock}`,\n59\t   check-and-set atomically BEFORE scheduling â€” resolves MAJOR S3-4 TOCTOU double-fire) + skip-if-running.\n60\t   The manual `POST /api/rnd/gandalf_run` endpoint is **NOT gated** by the module flag (manual is explicit).\n61\t5. **UI = a right-column \"Gandalf\" tab ABOVE Grass** (order: Gandalf â†’ Grass â†’ Deliverables). Run history\n62\t   newest-first; each row = one-line verdict + timestamp + a `degraded`/`cross_model` chip; clicking a row\n63\t   **expands the exec-summary INLINE** (mirror the cockpit accordion, not a page bounce â€” addresses S2-5),\n64\t   with `[Full report]` + `[raw JSON]` opening via the traversal-safe `/artifact` route. A **degraded/error\n65\t   run** renders an honest row (reason text, \"(no report)\" placeholder, no dead links â€” resolves minor\n66\t   S3-9). Honest empty state (\"No Gandalf read yet\" + a Run button) before the first run. A **white-wizard**\n67\t   icon (Gandalf the White â€” white robes/staff, NOT GWL green) = a new vendored SVG\n68\t   `vendor/brand/gandalf-white-icon.svg`, served by `/vendor/brand/`, **added to `dist_manifest.txt`**\n69\t   (resolves minor S3-7). HTML is f-string (double braces); panel JS in the RAW `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS`.\n70\t6. **Re-runnable any time**; each run a new timestamped entry; history accumulates newest-first.\n71\t\n72\t## Architecture â€” modules & seams (EXTEND, do not fork)\n73\t\n74\t### New: `gandalf.py` (stdlib only; in `dist_manifest.txt`)\n75\t- `run_gandalf(folder_path, project_id, *, force=False, env=None) -> dict` â€” build the embedded-protocol\n76\t  prompt â†’ `job_runner.launch_guarded`/`launch` with `cwd=folder`, `--add-dir folder`, the Gandalf timeout,\n77\t  the forwarded env â†’ `job_runner.extract_assistant_text` â†’ **locate the last balanced top-level JSON\n78\t  object + parse** â†’ **validate the schema contract** (9 required top-level keys + per-item required keys\n79\t  for any findings/elevations/risk_labels actually rendered â€” resolves MAJOR S3-3) â†’ render `report.md` +\n80\t  `exec-summary.md` â†’ write them + `advisor-output.json` to `gandalf/run-<ts>/` â†’ append a SAFE record to\n81\t  `.anchor/projects/<id>/gandalf/index.json` under `paths.WRITE_LOCK`. **Every run is stamped\n82\t  `degraded:true`** per the v1 honesty contract (the seam didn't run). A parse/validate/timeout failure is\n83\t  recorded as an honest **error run** (reason captured, no fabricated verdict, never raises to the caller).\n84\t- `run_gandalf_if_absent(folder_path, project_id, env=None)` â€” the first-scan idempotent no-op-if-prior-run.\n85\t- `list_runs(folder_path, project_id) -> list[dict]` â€” newest-first SAFE projections (ts Â· run_id Â·\n86\t  one-line verdict Â· cross_model Â· degraded Â· ok Â· report_rel Â· exec_rel Â· reason?). Never absolute paths.\n87\t- `get_run(...)`, render helpers `_render_full_report` / `_render_exec_summary` / `_one_line_verdict`\n88\t  (pinned to the top-level `verdict` field â€” resolves minor S1-6; defensive `.get()` everywhere).\n89\t- **Store/index** stamped with `GANDALF_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION`; `list_runs` normalizes older/missing\n90\t  versions with honest defaults (resolves minor S3-8).\n91\t\n92\t### Extend `anchor_gui.py`\n93\t- `POST /api/rnd/gandalf_run {project_id}` (token-authed) â†’ schedule a fresh run in a daemon thread\n94\t  (returns `{ok, scheduled:true}` immediately; in-flight guard; NOT module-flag-gated).\n95\t- `GET /api/rnd/gandalf?project_id=<id>` (`?token=`) â†’ `gandalf.list_runs` SAFE projection.\n96\t- `_trigger_gandalf(...)` (mirrors `_trigger_project_summary`) + the first-scan hook in the rescan block.\n97\t- `_render_layoutd_gandalf_panel(folder_path, project_id)` inserted in `_render_layoutd_html` BEFORE\n98\t  `{grass_panel}` in `<div class='rightcol'>` (`:3266`).\n99\t- `vendor/brand/gandalf-white-icon.svg` via the existing `/vendor/brand/` route.\n100\t\n101\t### Reuse unchanged\n102\t`job_runner` (launch + `extract_assistant_text` + `wait`), `report_viewer` (`/artifact`),\n103\t`paths.WRITE_LOCK`, `/vendor/brand/`, `summarizer.short_summary_text`.\n104\t\n105\t### CLI / healthcheck / distro / docs (PROJECT DONE wave)\n106\t- `anchor.py`: `rnd gandalf <pid>` â†’ `gandalf.list_runs` (read-only, newest-first, honest-absent). No\n107\t  mutating CLI form (run/re-run is interactive).\n108\t- `anchor_healthcheck.check_gandalf_surface` â€” fully stubbed (`ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD` â†’ `tests/stub_gandalf.py`\n109\t  + temp data/git dirs + `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY` off): run â†’ 3 artifacts + index â†’ `list_runs` shape â†’\n110\t  re-run appends a 2nd entry â†’ a degraded/unparseable run recorded honestly. **Snapshots+restores\n111\t  `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD` + `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY`, registers temp dirs in `rnd_env[\"v3_temp_dirs\"]`,\n112\t  registered in `main()` after `check_rnd_v12_surface`** (resolves minor S3-6). Never binds `:8777`.\n113\t- `distro.py`: `gandalf.py` + the SVG in `dist_manifest.txt`; import scan green (assert the SVG manifest\n114\t  entry in the distro test).\n115\t- `CLAUDE.md` + `SESSION-HANDOFF.md` updated.\n116\t- **Live-smoke (manual, NOT a pytest gate â€” needs real claude):** before declaring prod done, one real\n117\t  `claude -p` Gandalf run on a representative project must emit parseable schema JSON within the timeout\n118\t  (resolves the prod-path half of BLOCKER B / S1-1). Documented as a deploy checklist item.\n119\t\n120\t## Hard constraints (carried, non-negotiable)\n121\t- Python stdlib only (lone lazy `pywinpty` waiver); `gandalf.py` stdlib-only + manifest; distro scan green.\n122\t- Hermetic tests: `tests/stub_gandalf.py` (one compact schema JSON in a `result` envelope), temp git/data\n123\t  dirs, `ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub` where PTY touched, `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY` off; NEVER bind `:8777` /\n124\t  real data / network / real claude / the real Skill-Foundry skill.\n125\t- Playwright DEV-ONLY (`pytest.importorskip`), never imported by product code.\n126\t- `anchor_gui.py` HTML f-string (double braces); `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` RAW single-brace; render-smoke before\n127\t  any Playwright wave.\n128\t- UI wave GREEN = rendered-DOM (pos+neg) + a real Playwright+Chromium interaction test (machine-checkable) +\n129\t  an orchestrator screenshot vs the Gandalf-tab mockup + John's sign-off. NO merge / NO `nssm restart`\n130\t  until John signs off. Every wave holds or grows the test count.\n131\t\n132\t## Risks & mitigations (post-Shark-Tank)\n133\t- **R1 â€” schema parse/validate fragility.** Extract assistant text â†’ last balanced top-level JSON object â†’\n134\t  validate the named contract; on any failure â†’ honest error run (reason), never crash. Stub-tested happy\n135\t  AND degraded paths.\n136\t- **R2 â€” first-scan cost.** Pointing at the folder is an unbounded agentic run; first-run-ONLY +\n137\t  background daemon + module-flag-gated + a Gandalf-specific timeout. Honest that prod first-scan WILL\n138\t  auto-fire one run per newly-registered project (decision #4).\n139\t- **R3 â€” render-path blocking.** The tab/CLI read `index.json` only; generation is always a daemon thread.\n140\t- **R4 â€” same-model honesty / un-seamed run.** Every run stamped `degraded:true` + `cross_model:false`,\n141\t  surfaced as chips (the v1 honesty contract); never dressed up as full-rigor.\n142\t- **R5 â€” artifact serving.** Served artifacts live at PROJECT ROOT `gandalf/` (NOT `.anchor`, which\n143\t  `/artifact` rejects) via the existing traversal-safe route; the internal index is never served.\n144\t- **R6 â€” concurrent/double first-scan.** Per-project in-process lock check-and-set BEFORE scheduling +\n145\t  skip-if-running + atomic index writes under `paths.WRITE_LOCK`; a concurrency test asserts â‰¤1 run.\n146\t- **R7 â€” token-auth/traversal.** New endpoints token-authed; artifacts only via `/artifact` (project-rel).\n147\t\n148\t## Out of scope (Grasscatched for a possible v2)\n149\t- **Full Node-seam Gandalf rigor** (deterministic tier validation / canary harness in the loop) â€” v1 is\n150\t  honestly degraded. Cross-model/Enhanced substrate; auto-run on every rescan; global cross-project Gandalf\n151\t  view; diffing two runs; turning a Gandalf finding into an effort/grass idea.\n152\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"345402c6-3af5-432b-85c9-f2708dfa1cf2","uuid":"e6883b6a-0431-44eb-96dd-992c14ff58cf","timestamp":"2026-06-23